Open Burp Suite → Proxy → Intercept → turn ON
Set browser proxy: IP 127.0.0.1, Port 8080
Proxy → Options → Import/export CA certificate → export DER format → install in browser
Open app login page → enter credentials → click Login → request captured in Burp
In captured request, observe:

POST /rest/user/login HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:3000
{"email": "user@test.com", "password": "123456"}

Modify values to:

json{"email": "admin@test.com", "password": "admin123"}

Click Forward → observe response (status, token)
Intercept other requests (profile, orders) → modify userId, role, price
Change amount value in a request:

json{"amount": 1}

Forward and observe behavior
